          "create_time": 1792861204.336,
          "update_time": 1792861206.435,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "\\(m_a\\) is the **multiplicity (order) of the zero at \\(z=a\\)** of \\(H(t,z)\\), with \\(t\\) fixed. Locally,\n\\[\nH(t,z)=(z-a)^{m_a}g(z),\\qquad g(a)\\ne0.\n\\]\nThus a simple zero has \\(m_a=1\\), a double zero has \\(m_a=2\\), and so on.\n\nIn [equation `eq:divisor`](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-4/12_height_dependent_heat_contours/manuscript/book.tex:133), \\(\\delta_a\\) is a unit point mass at \\(a\\). The equation says that, as \\(\\epsilon\\downarrow0\\), the smooth density concentrates at the zeros, assigning each zero mass equal to its multiplicity."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
          "metadata": {
            "source": "Codex completed public message",
            "source_turn_id": "01a16eda-4f27-7f61-bd3e-37ec6f4e1c35",
